# bothy-web builds from THIS directory, and the Dockerfile COPYs only
# nginx.conf and web/. An allowlist, like apps/.dockerignore, so a new
# directory here cannot quietly join the context.
#
# web/node_modules is the one that matters: the Dockerfile runs `npm ci` and
# then `COPY web/ ./`, so a host node_modules in the context would be laid over
# the locked install and the build would ship whatever the box had. web/dist
# likewise. data/ changes every minute (the collector writes it) and is
# bind-mounted, never baked.
*
!Dockerfile
!nginx.conf
!web
web/node_modules
web/dist
web/.vite
web/.mdcheck-tmp
web/*.tsbuildinfo
